menu "Michi Music Stream Button"

    config MICHI_BUTTON_DEBOUNCE_MS
        int "Debounce window (ms)"
        default 20
        range 5 200
        help
          Stable-window debounce: an edge (press/release) is confirmed only
          after the pin stays at the same level for this long
          (DEBOUNCE_MS/POLL_MS consecutive samples). 20 ms rejects the
          bounce of a typical tactile button; contacts that bounce longer
          need a larger window.

    config MICHI_BUTTON_LONG_PRESS_MS
        int "Long press threshold (ms)"
        default 5000
        range 500 30000
        help
          Press duration (measured edge-to-edge from the ISR timestamps) at
          or above which the press counts as LONG and runs
          MICHI_BUTTON_LONG_PRESS_ACTION instead of pairing. 5 s is long
          enough that a normal pairing tap can never trip it, short enough
          to be practical as a recovery/factory-reset gesture.

    choice MICHI_BUTTON_LONG_PRESS_ACTION
        prompt "Long press action"
        default MICHI_BUTTON_LONG_PRESS_RECOVERY
        help
          What a long press (>= MICHI_BUTTON_LONG_PRESS_MS) does. Both
          actions are ignored while the FSM is in BOOTING, SELF_TEST or
          UPDATING.

        config MICHI_BUTTON_LONG_PRESS_RECOVERY
            bool "Recovery: post MICHI_EVENT_RECOVER"
            help
              Posts MICHI_EVENT_RECOVER, which drives RECOVERABLE_ERROR ->
              IDLE (event mapping in michi_state). Safe in every state; the
              FSM only applies it from RECOVERABLE_ERROR.

        config MICHI_BUTTON_LONG_PRESS_FACTORY_RESET
            bool "Factory reset: erase NVS + restart"
            help
              Erases the NVS partition (network profile, DAC override,
              device id, ...) and restarts. DESTRUCTIVE: all stored
              settings are lost. Blocked while UPDATING so a long press
              can never brick an OTA in progress.
    endchoice

    config MICHI_BUTTON_POLL_MS
        int "Debounce task poll period (ms)"
        default 10
        range 1 100
        help
          Sampling period of the debounce task. 10 ms gives sub-tick
          resolution for the press duration while keeping the task at 100
          samples/s of a single GPIO read.

    config MICHI_BUTTON_TASK_STACK_BYTES
        int "Debounce task stack (bytes)"
        default 3072
        range 2048 16384
        help
          Stack of the debounce task (ESP-IDF xTaskCreate takes bytes).
          The task polls one GPIO and posts events, so the default is
          generous.

endmenu
